From 9745b4cbc9b373355c873ea7a3e65b6c2caf1867 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:07:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] openvpn: the 2.7.8 security fixes backported onto 2.7.7

From OpenVPN 2.7.8 (2026-10-07): CVE-2026-88964, an unsigned underflow
when a pushed domain_search_list is cleared; CVE-2026-84790, certificate
subjects with embedded NUL bytes accepted on both the OpenSSL and mbed TLS
verify paths; the wrapped-key resend fix and the pushed-epoch tag check in
init.c (upstream d586f8ad9bfc, cf4384eef467, b0cb5029b2d9, 69a7cb1b4f87,
applied with patch -p1, unit tests included). The ssl.c block that
returned KEY_GEN_FAILED, an enum 2.7.7 lacks, keeps 2.7.7's M_FATAL with a
comment. The reported version stays 2.7.7; the full 2.7.8 import is for
the next component rung. REAPER-FIXES C19.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
